==Battleground==
*1 [[Crazed Bird Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Bird Cat]] spawns as the boss.
*1 [[Crazed Axe Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Axe Cat]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*3 [[Crazed Gross Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Gross Cats]] spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 36.67~40 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,200f</sup>.
*4 [[Crazed Gross Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Gross Cats]] spawn after 153.33 seconds<sup>4,600f</sup>, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.

==Strategy ==
[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] is almost mandatory for this stage, as it can block Crazed Gross's [[Wave Attack]]s while also weakening Crazed Bird Cat later on. Players must be cautious, however, as Octopus tends to die easily thanks to Crazed Axe. Hard-hitting Cats that are [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immune]] such as [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Miyamoku Musashi]] are great assets here; keep them behind Octopus and your meatshield lines to break down the Crazed Axe and Crazed Bird over time.

The Crazed Gross Cats are the only consistent income source, and they will stop spawning after a while, so care must be paid to money. A Rich Cat may help a good deal in this stage.

[[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|Anti-Traitless Cats]] such as [[Driller Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Power Driller]] and [[Shadow Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Shadow Gao]] can be quite useful here.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Supercat]]: Tends to be frozen in place by [[Crazed Axe Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Axe Cat]] allowing him to block the waves more consistently than [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] as the knockback puts him out of every enemy range in the stage. At the same time, every hit he makes weakens [[Crazed Axe Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Axe Cat]] and [[Crazed Gross Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Gross Cats]] making them a lot easier to deal with.
*[[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]]: Due to the low number of enemies and relatively easy stalling, sniper can constantly gain ground by knocking back the enemy. After stalling long enough to get 2 of them out it becomes basically impossible to lose, unless they're hit by Crazed Gross's Wave.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]: Same reason as Sniper, even better if combined with Sniper the Deadeye.
*[[Brainwashed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed King Dragon Cat]]: Since the usual way to beat this stage uberless is to stack dragons, having a Dragon variant that is immune to both the Waves and Freeze of the enemies helps a lot. Beware that they're unlocked pretty late into the game.
*[[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Vendor Cat and Kitten]]: Capable of regaining ground lost to Crazed Axe due to it's immunity to freeze, though beware of the fact that Crazed Bird can easily kill it.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Ninja Girl Tomoe (Uber Rare Cat)|Ninja Girl Tomoe]]: Though unable to freeze the [[Crazed Bird Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Bird Cat]], she can be combined with other anti-Traitless crowd-controllers to stop the Crazed Axe and Gross Cats.
*Ranged Wave Shields like [[EVA Unit-00 (Uber Rare Cat)]], who can invalidate some of this stage's gimmick entirely, although it is recommended you bring other waveblockers since crazed bird and axe both outrange it.
*Anti-traitless ubers that are [[Immune to Waves]] or [[Immune to Freeze]], can make this stage trivial, such as [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|D'arktanyan]]. Do be aware that you'll need to meatshield a lot for him to be effective. [[Lone Moon Lunos (Uber Rare Cat)|Lone Moon Lunos]] however, excels here, he can tank everything here with relative ease as he can both knockback and is resistant to Traitless and Floating.

